  },
  "claim": {
    "statement": "Under sustained load, the substrate stays cognitively alive on real input: \u25a1 (for every cycle that produced a concept set, \u03a6 \u2265 0.05). Empty-concept cycles are excluded \u2014 with nothing to integrate, \u03a6=0 is correct, not a defect; their rate is reported separately. The floor is the lowest-\u03a6 real-input cycle across the run.",
    "operationalization": "Stream 3 passes over 8 substantive stimuli through Kimera's entity target (Takwin); read the per-cycle ``phi`` and ``concepts``. Partition cycles into real-input (concepts non-empty) and empty-input. phi_floor = min \u03a6 over real-input cycles; the LTL \u25a1 invariant holds iff that floor \u2265 \u03c6_floor. empty_input_rate and the over-all-cycles phi_floor_strict are reported alongside.",
    "threshold": {
      "metric": "phi_floor",
      "comparator": ">=",
      "value": 0.05,
      "units": "phi"
    },
    "h0": "H0: min \u03a6 < 0.05 on real-input cycles \u2014 \u03a6 collapses below the floor despite the input producing concepts",
    "h1": "H1: min \u03a6 \u2265 0.05 on real-input cycles \u2014 the substrate stays cognitively alive whenever it has something to integrate"
  },
  "preregistration": {
    "config_hash": "fc0d6fa2b433540d0fc987795a9290da4c1acaff4c0266fcacf945fe8d7490b4",
    "data_hash": "0289f594eb2ea25b582960992cf2db41bf790750618ae39f5dadc693ee1fb06b",
    "analysis_plan": "Build a sustained-load schedule (3 passes over 8 stimuli = 24 cycles); stream it through Kimera's entity target. Read per-cycle \u03a6 + concepts; partition into real-input vs empty-input cycles. Decide the LTL \u25a1 invariant on real-input cycles: min \u03a6 \u2265 0.05. Report empty_input_rate + phi_floor_strict (over all cycles) alongside. INCONCLUSIVE if fewer than 6 real-input cycles. The \u03a6 band, per-pass means, and per-cycle \u03a6 series are descriptive; none post-hoc-claimable.",
    "sweep_grid": {},
    "preregistered_at": "2026-05-21T23:40:38.828736+00:00"
  },
